.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Frenkel (1926) argued that at any T&gt;0 some ions leave their sites for interstitial gaps, because the configurational entropy gained outweighs the enthalpy cost at low concentration. The equilibrium number is n_F=\sqrt{NN_i}\exp(-\Delta H_F/2k_BT) (~chemistrykit.crystal.systems.defects.frenkel_defect_concentration). AgCl, where small Ag+ ions readily occupy interstitial sites, is the textbook Frenkel-dominated solid (\Delta H_F\approx1.4 eV).">

